API Gateway
--- So far so real good we have built three services, establish a sync comm.  between two services, and then create a service registry where all service registers and are commuted via the discovery server. To access a particular service, we go directly to the endpoint and access it(e.g order service[localhost:5051/api/order] etc), while this is cool for a local dev. env. this pose security risk to the microservices and isn't suitable for a prod. env. Also, since a microservice can have multiple instances running concurrently, we cannot afford to have the endpoint of those instances expose to the outside world.
--- We introduce the concept of API gateway. which is responsible for routing request from user/client to the corresponding services. It acts like an entry point into the system landscape, if the user wants to call the product service, the user calls the API gateway, with the url(like onlineshop.com) and to be able to call the product service, it will be onlineshop.com/api/product.
--- In our API gateway we can configure the rules such that if it recieves a request with /api/product then route it to product service, similarly with /api/order then the request should be routed to the order service, and other service endpoint rules configuration. 
-- The api gateway act as a gatekeeper to whatever request the user want to make to the services.

--- The API gateway also address cross cutting concerns like routing based on request header as discuss earlier, authentication(if we want ensure authentication of all the request, we can configure that in the api gateway, the api gateway will interact with the authorization server configured whether it is the keycloak authentication server), Load balancer(the api gateway can also act as a load balancer, if we have multiple instance of the product service for instance, if the user makes a request to the product service, it will ensure it calls the less busy instance of the service and retrieve the response of that instance and sends it to the user), SSL termination(if we include the TLS/SSL scheme in our request to one of the service, since we don't need the https in the services as it is an internal comm., the api gateway will terminate the ssl in the incoming request. if we send a request to the order service via the API gateway using https://onlineshop.com/api/order, the api gateway will automatically terminate the ssl in https and route the request to the respective service.) 

--- There are many types of API gateway like ApiGee, but we will make use of SPRING CLOUD GATEWAY. We can visit the spring-cloud url to learn more about the spring cloud gateway. To get strarted we will go to the favorite website and get the dependency information(we copy the spring cloud routing dep.). next we create a new module in our maven project, and add the dep. to the pom xml file. 
--- Next we will create a new package(com.ShoppingMS.ApiGateway) and create a class in the minion package(ApiGatewayApplication), then we add the @SpringBootApplication to the class and the main minions. Next we want to add a dep. for discovery client, since the api gateway is also a component inside the microservice landscape, therefore we copy the eureka client dep. from any of the service pom and paste in the api gateway pom, this automatically makes it a discovery client(or we can add the @EnableDiscoveryClient for best practice).
--- Next, we will create the app.prop file and add the discovery server url so that it can register it self on start up. Some additional information will be added to prop file(SEE CODE). In the prop file we configure the logging of the API gateway such that we get full info on what is happening behind the scenes when a request is made. Also in the prop file we define the routes for the various services(SEE CODE oya, lb means loadbalancer(the api gateway will perform client side load balancing)). Specify the port 8080 in the prop file since it is the default gateway.
-- On most Unix-based systems (Linux, macOS), only ports >= 1024 are allowed to be used by non-root users. Ports below 1024 are restricted.
